From d89d9d4e3291bc770028a67e7c6aa9459e40ede9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:27:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/26] arm64: dts: rk3566-pinetab2: limit the OTG port to full
 speed

With 0009 the gadget finally drives D+ and the host sees the device, but
enumeration still dies immediately:

    host:   usb 1-1: new high-speed USB device number 126 using xhci_hcd
            usb 1-1: device descriptor read/64, error -71
    device: dwc3_event: Reset [U0]
            dwc3_event: Connection Done [U0]
            ep0out/ep0in 'Set Endpoint Configuration' --> Successful
            dwc3_event: Erratic Error [U0]
            dwc3_event: Erratic Error [U0]   (~115 per second, forever)

Reset and chirp both succeed and ep0 is armed, then the core reports the
PHY is handing it invalid line states and the host's first SETUP never
arrives. Forcing DCFG.devspd to full speed at runtime - nothing else
changed - enumerates instantly and completely:

    usb 1-1: new full-speed USB device number 11
    usb 1-1: Product: LuneOS Device
    cdc_ether 1-1:1.0 usb0: CDC Ethernet Device

so the gadget, the DT and dwc3 are all fine; only the USB2 high-speed
physical layer is broken on this port.

The following were all measured on the device and made no difference at
high speed (each retried with a fresh RUN_STOP cycle):

  - PHY HS eye height (0x30 bits 6:4) swept 0,1,4,6,7
  - PHY differential receiver (0x30 bit 2) on and off
  - PHY pre-emphasis (0x00 bits 2:0) swept 0,1,2,4,7
  - GUSB2PHYCFG dis_enblslpm and dis-u2-freeclk-exists
  - GUCTL1 parkmode-disable-hs and tx-ipgap-linecheck-dis
  - DCFG LPM_CAP off

and the configuration the driver does apply is confirmed correct in
hardware: RK3568 PHY tuning present (0x00=0x04, 0x400=0x04, 0x30=0x61),
GUSB2PHYCFG SUSPHY=0 PHYIF=16-bit USBTRDTIM=5, GUCTL refclkper=41ns,
GFLADJ 240MHz-decr=10, GRF opmode=0 phy_sus=0 bvalid=1 avalid=1 id=1.
The OTG and host port register blocks of usb2phy0 are byte-identical
apart from the deliberate 0x30 tuning.

Insensitivity to every analog knob, combined with chirp succeeding and
clocked data failing, points at the board rather than the SoC. Cap the
port at full speed so USB networking and MTP work at all; drop this
patch if the high-speed path is ever fixed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hardware-specific workaround]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
index 5fde8afb13fb..3ab19bf0537d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -1002,6 +1002,7 @@ &usb_host0_ohci {
 /* OTG port controller */
 &usb_host0_xhci {
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	maximum-speed = "full-speed";
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
